## Summary
The article reports that the Korean sea is experiencing the highest rate of warming globally, with sea level rise approximately twice the world average. This indicates significant and accelerated climate change impacts on the region's marine environment.

## Key Points
- The Korean sea has the highest warming rate among global seas.
- Sea level rise in the area is occurring at twice the global average rate.
- This phenomenon is a clear indicator of severe climate change effects on marine ecosystems.


